2. He went voluntarily and of his own accord to the Garden, which answered the Adduction or bringing of the Beast to be Sacrificed unto the Door of the Tabernacle according to the Law; for there he did not only give up himself into the hands of those who were to shed his Blood;
but also actually entred upon the offering up of himself unto God in his
Agony, when he offered up Prayers and Supplications with strong Crying and Tears, Heb. 5. 7. which declares not the Matter but the Manner of his Offering.
